## Filter shorthand reference

The `filter_entity` + `filter_field` shorthand resolves to an internal Turbonomic `filterType` at plan time. Supported combinations:

| `filter_entity` | `filter_field` | Resolved `filterType` |
|---|---|---|
| `vm` | `name` | `vmsByName` |
| `vm` | `tag` | `vmsByTag` |
| `vm` | `state` | `vmsByState` |
| `vm` | `guest_os` | `vmsByGuestName` |
| `vm` | `cloud_provider` | `vmsByCloudProvider` |
| `vm` | `pm` | `vmsByPMName` |
| `vm` | `cluster` | `vmsByClusterName` |
| `vm` | `dc` | `vmsByDCnested` |
| `vm` | `vdc` | `vmsByVDC` |
| `vm` | `network` | `vmsByNetwork` |
| `vm` | `storage` | `vmsByStorage` |
| `vm` | `business_account` | `vmsByBusinessAccountUuid` |
| `pm` | `name` | `pmsByName` |
| `pm` | `tag` | `pmsByTag` |
| `pm` | `state` | `pmsByState` |
| `pm` | `cluster` | `pmsByClusterName` |
| `storage` | `name` | `storageByName` |
| `storage` | `tag` | `storageByTag` |
| `storage` | `state` | `storageByState` |
| `storage` | `pm_cluster` | `storageByPMCluster` |
| `db` | `name` | `databaseByName` |
| `db` | `tag` | `databaseByTag` |
| `db` | `cloud_provider` | `databaseByCloudProvider` |
| `db` | `business_account` | `databaseByBusinessAccountUuid` |
| `db_server` | `name` | `databaseServerByName` |
| `db_server` | `tag` | `databaseServerByTag` |
| `db_server` | `business_account` | `databaseServerByBusinessAccountUuid` |
| `container` | `name` | `containersByName` |
| `container` | `namespace` | `containersByNamespace` |
| `namespace` | `name` | `namespacesByName` |
| `cluster` | `name` | `clustersByName` |
| `cluster` | `tag` | `clustersByTag` |
| `storage_cluster` | `name` | `storageClustersByName` |
| `vm_cluster` | `name` | `virtualMachineClustersByName` |
| `container_platform_cluster` | `name` | `containerPlatformClustersByName` |
| `resource_group` | `name` | `resourceGroupByName` |
| `resource_group` | `tag` | `resourceGroupByTag` |
| `resource_group` | `business_account` | `resourceGroupByBusinessAccountUuid` |
| `business_account` | `name` | `businessAccountByName` |
| `volume` | `storage` | `volumeByStorage` |
| `volume` | `resource_group` | `volumeByResourceGroupName` |

For filter combinations not listed here, set `filter_type` directly with the raw Turbonomic filter key.

## Notes

- **Static vs dynamic.** Set `is_static = true` and populate `member_uuid_list` for a fixed membership group. Set `is_static = false` (default) and populate `criteria_list` for a dynamic membership group.
- **`filter_type` is resolved at plan time.** When `filter_entity` + `filter_field` are set, `ModifyPlan` computes `filter_type` before apply so the plan has no unknown values.
- **`logical_operator` applies across all criteria.** All criteria in a single group are joined by the same operator (`AND`, `OR`, or `XOR`).
- **`environment_type` and `cloud_type` are computed.** These fields are derived by Turbonomic from the group members and cannot be set in configuration.
- **Import.** Import an existing group using its UUID: `terraform import turbonomic_group.example <uuid>`.

